# agent worktrees + session config -- never commit
.claude/

# build artifacts -- NEVER commit these. Two stale v0.1.0 files were tracked under dist/,
# and because CI runs `python -m build` into the SAME dist/ and then uploads dist/*
# wholesale, every tagged release tried to re-publish quiverlab-0.1.0 to PyPI, got a
# 400 "File already exists" and aborted BEFORE the real version uploaded. That is why
# 0.3.0 and 1.0.0 never reached PyPI. (`desktop/dist/` above is a different tree.)
/dist/
/build/
*.egg-info/

# Root-level scratch: browser "Save As" pages (each drops a `<name>_files/` asset
# dir, sometimes with third-party tracker JS) and stray report/compute PDFs+HTML.
# ~43 such files were committed at the repo root and got untracked for v1.0.1.
# Anchored with a leading `/` to the repo ROOT ONLY, so the curated `for-maths/`
# worked-example set (*.html/*.json/*.pdf + its README) and any docs/ HTML stay
# tracked.
/*.html
/*.pdf
/*_files/
